343:
Let it fly across the world;
I give this song to you,
this little song about five minutes.

348:
Five minutes, five minutes,
the clock will soon be striking;
if you've quarreled, make your peace.

352:
The New Year won't wait;
it's almost at our door.
Five minutes will fly by;
there's so little time left.

359:
Five minutes isn't long;
he's on the right track;
his road is a good one.

486:
- Comrades, your attention
for a moment! Come on, everyone,
let's stop laughing!

497:
The night, just as before,
hangs stars across the sky;
the waltz plays, now sad, now gay.

515:
look into each other's eyes;
sometimes a glance says more
than any words.
